sequenceDiagram
    actor Streamer as Streamer (OBS)
    participant NGX as Nginx-RTMP
    participant SRS as SRS Server
    participant FFmpeg as FFmpeg
    participant HLS as Nginx HLS
    participant WebRTC as SRS WebRTC
    participant Broker as RabbitMQ
    participant Consumer as Consumer Service
    actor Viewer as Espectador

    Note over NGX,SRS: Implementação A (Nginx-RTMP) ou B (SRS) — configurável

    alt Implementação A: Nginx-RTMP
        Streamer->>NGX: Stream RTMP (1080p) :1935
        NGX->>NGX: Valida Stream Key (callback HTTP → /api/streams/callback/publish)
        NGX->>FFmpeg: exec transcode-ffmpeg.sh {key}
    else Implementação B: SRS
        Streamer->>SRS: Stream RTMP (1080p) :1935
        SRS->>SRS: Valida Stream Key (callback HTTP → /api/streams/callback/publish)
        SRS->>FFmpeg: exec transcode-ffmpeg.sh {key}
        SRS->>WebRTC: Conversão RTMP → WebRTC nativa
    end

    FFmpeg->>FFmpeg: Transcodifica 4 qualidades (1080p/720p/480p/360p)
    FFmpeg->>HLS: Segmentos .ts + master.m3u8 → /tmp/hls/{key}/

    NGX->>Broker: Evento stream_started
    SRS->>Broker: Evento stream_started
    Consumer->>Broker: Consome evento
    Consumer->>Consumer: Atualiza métricas

    alt Protocolo HLS (Impl A ou B)
        Viewer->>HLS: GET /hls/{key}/master.m3u8
        HLS-->>Viewer: Playlist com 4 variantes de qualidade
        Viewer->>HLS: GET segmentos .ts (adaptive bitrate)
        HLS-->>Viewer: Vídeo HLS (~3–10s latência)
    else Protocolo WebRTC (apenas Impl B — SRS)
        Viewer->>WebRTC: Conexão WebRTC (SDP offer)
        WebRTC-->>Viewer: Stream em tempo real (~100–300ms latência)
    end
